# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Due to the lack of the onlyOwner modifier in _authorizeUpgrade, any caller can arbitrarily switch the implementation in the Aquifer contract.  
This could lead to the proxy being upgraded to a Well contract implementation against the Owner's wishes. Attackers could also choose to upgrade to a deprecated Well implementation.  
Additionally, the Aquifer factory has not implemented security checks, which introduces a new attack vector.  
## Proof of Concept
The UUPS proxy pattern manages access control through the _authorizeUpgrade function.
The _authorizeUpgrade function restricts the implementation during proxy upgrades to those registered through the Aquifer factory, but it does not impose any restrictions on the caller.  

